KG42.register("clusters-c063db8e59e8f795d0a692aa",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v142-d-CL003","paper":"31-coalition_formation","label":"State-specific pricing and battery energy trading execution","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"State-specific pricing and battery energy trading execution","market_meaning":"Under the conditions of the selected coalition and provider/receiver quantities, state 1 adopts the cited mid-market scheme, state 2 determines the transaction price based on total-quantity balance and the charging/discharging price relationship, and executes battery energy exchange within the coalition. Transactions must simultaneously satisfy their respective state boundaries and battery/network constraints; the baseline excludes selling state 2 battery energy to CPS, and the case of CPS as a peer is retained only as a conditional extension.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["activation","pricing","clearing","matching"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"Pricing and execution have explicit price and energy interfaces; the two states and the CPS baseline/extension are retained separately. The execution upper bound, positive energy-deficit branching, state 2 price version and parameter basis after member adjustment still conflict, so it cannot be concluded that this combination can be directly executed.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This cluster is assembled around at what price and under what feasible conditions transactions are executed within the selected coalition. How the coalition forms serves only as a shared interface, and clearing balance only as a shared obligation; the primary attribution of these chains is not reacquired, nor is shared balance counted again as an independent rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the state branches, intra-coalition execution, physical feasibility constraints and the CPS baseline and extension boundaries."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the initial price and state 2 transaction price, the line-cost price relationship and the battery degradation incentive principle; prices at different stages remain separate."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Share C001 and its total-quantity object as the state 2 balance obligation jointly adopted by execution and pricing; this cluster does not reassert that the allocation algorithm has achieved balance."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Share the member results, provider/receiver conditions and the process interface for transfer into V, and use its energy-deficit branching condition to check execution feasibility; these conditions still conflict and are not treated as satisfied preconditions."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C010"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-M01-E24"],"rationale":"Within the common condition scope of having previously belonged to W and currently selecting V, the split/merge operation of the matching chain connects with the transaction after transfer into coalition 2 recorded by the execution chain; the broader member-transition conditions are not regarded as completely identical expressions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pd-s2","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pc-s2","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-M01-E24"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that coalition 2 uses the prices of equations (18)-(19), so the pricing output with the s2 subscript corresponds to the execution price requirement; the extraction conflict in equation (19) remains, and it is not merged with the initial general price object."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E31"],"rationale":"The two chains restate the same total-quantity balance obligation within the same state 2 provider/receiver scope, used respectively for clearing and execution; retain the two functional attributions and do not count an additional independent balance rule."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Ed","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Ec","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-Ed","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-Ec","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"],"rationale":"The same state 2 charging/discharging totals and balance conditions are used for price calculation; this establishes only a quantity-and-condition interface and does not prove that the item-by-item reduction step or the constrained individual response satisfies the closed-form pricing assumptions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E26"],"rationale":"The degradation compensation and trading incentive principles, together with the design's restriction on same-slot cross-state trading, are different scopes of action of the same price design in the source; retain their given model conditions and do not expand them into a general conclusion prohibiting cross-state trading."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-CN06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x_e_nd","v141-c-R004::x::x_e_nc","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C016"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_end","v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_enc","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E38"],"rationale":"The same state 2 battery charging/discharging quantity must be positive in the member definition and is also constrained by equation (7) in the execution chain. This interface is used to expose the intersection problem between eligibility and the feasible region, and does not claim that all selected members can execute."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The same frozen pricing node serves member selection and transaction pricing; only the node display is unified, not the price quantities at each stage or their applicable conditions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-M01-E24"],"rationale":"The two places reference the same frozen matching node, covering respectively the interfaces of member reorganization and post-reorganization execution; transition constraints with different scopes are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R007::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"],"rationale":"The two places reference the same frozen clearing node and are displayed as the same functional object; the total-quantity balance objective and its price use are still retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM04","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E31"],"rationale":"Both require the total provider discharge and total receiver charge within V in the same time period to be equal, with consistent meaning and scope, so one may be selected for display; all original constraints are retained. R007-C001 additionally contains price calculation and is not included in whole-item deduplication."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Ed","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-Ed"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"],"rationale":"Both are the total discharge of the same state 2 provider set, serving respectively as the clearing balance quantity and as a price-calculation input; retain the units, definitional descriptions and local representations, and do not conclude on this basis that the values in different adjustment stages are equal."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Ec","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-Ec"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"],"rationale":"Both are the total charging of the same state 2 receiver set, with different clearing and pricing uses; retain the original objects, and which stage's total is actually adopted still needs to be clarified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_end","v141-c-R004::x::x_e_nd"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E38"],"rationale":"The source uses the same state 2 battery discharge quantity for the upper bound in equation (7) and the provider definition in equation (21); retain the role and unit differences between the execution-feasible quantity and the member-test quantity; the quantity correspondence does not eliminate the constraint conflict."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-OM08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_enc","v141-c-R004::x::x_e_nc"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E38"],"rationale":"The source uses the same state 2 battery charge quantity for the upper bound in equation (7) and the receiver definition in equation (20); do not rewrite its local role, units or member conditions, and do not thereby resolve the n/m indexing problem in Algorithm 1."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All assembly relationships have only experimental candidate eligibility, and the cited B evidence has still not undergone source audit; source-version conflicts cannot be regarded as resolved by the current assembly selection.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the execution restrictions, price expressions and their conditions, and independently review cross-chain feasibility."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The max definition retained in equation (8) is inconsistent with the textual requirement not to exceed both the battery rated rate and the network upper limit at the same time. The frozen expression alone cannot guarantee satisfaction of the two upper limits or protection of the stated voltage limit.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C011","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_R003_emax","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_R003_Echrdis","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_R003_Etransfer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g02-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the printed definition and textual intent of equation (8), and have upstream clarify the restriction actually adopted; D keeps the max expression unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"If the same time period and the same residual energy-deficit basis are adopted, the discharge upper bound in equation (7) makes positive discharge require positive E_{n,def}(t), whereas Algorithm 1 first places positive energy-deficit parties in W. Directly concatenating them in this way would exclude state 2 positive-discharge providers, and the member-selection result cannot be directly regarded as satisfying the execution upper bound.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_end","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C013","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C016","v141-c-R004::x::x_E_def"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E38"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the meaning, applicable objects, and computation timing of each quantity in Eq. (7) and lines 16-21 of the algorithm; first clarify whether they are the same shortage quantity, then have the upstream handle conditional conflicts, without independently swapping the upper bound or changing the diversion rules."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The state-2 closed-form price depends on the energy responses in Eqs. (14)-(16), but these responses do not enter the frozen chain as complete constraints, nor is the applicability after the upper bound in Eq. (7) takes effect explained. The handling of empty supplier-recipient sets, zero denominators, and response truncation is incomplete; some symbols in Eq. (7) are not typed, and the energy/rated-rate units and non-negativity domains are not unified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_enc","v141-c-R003::x::x_R003_end","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C016"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should supplement source-supported responses and applicable conditions, clarify empty sets, constraint activation, and unit conventions; independently check whether the aggregate price solution can yield quantities that satisfy individual execution limits."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G05","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"s_{n,d}(t), b_{m,c}(t), and s_{m,c}(t) lack explicit independent definitions. Eq. (5) already interprets b_{n,c}(t) as available capacity, whereas the subsequent receiving response again subtracts SoC; whether the change in subscripts accompanies a change in meaning is unclear, and they cannot be automatically merged with total capacity or other SoC objects.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-s-n-d","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-b-m-c","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-s-m-c","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the definitions of battery capacity and state quantities in each equation and the meaning of their subscripts; before the definitions are confirmed, retain the original objects and do not establish same-quantity mappings merely because the symbols are similar."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G06","category":"unverified_source","description":"g02-E33 and g03-E04 give opposite versions of the position of (1+β) in Eq. (19). What R007 currently freezes is the multiplicative relation consistent with Eq. (17), but this choice has not yet passed source auditing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pc-s2"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original Eq. (19) and handle the two extracted versions; retain the current C expression and the conflicting evidence citations, and do not create or replace formulas in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G07","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"After quantity reduction and member removal, it is unclear whether the K, L, and aggregate battery state used in the pricing formula are recalculated; the initial general price and the price with the s2 subscript are also not determined to be the same object or to have an explicit update relation. Identical symbols are insufficient to prove cross-stage numerical consistency.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-K","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-L","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pd","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pd-s2","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g02-E32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the computation stage for the member set, counts, aggregate quantities, and battery state used in pricing, as well as the relationship between the initial and final prices; display representatives or same-quantity mappings must not substitute for stage update rules."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G08","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The baseline exclusion in R003-C009 and the CPS in C010 as a peer extension must apply separately. The extension provides only a qualitative statement that trading is permitted when a negotiable price exists, and does not provide specific matching, pricing, or settlement rules.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g03-E05"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The baseline continues to remain excluded; if the CPS extension needs to be implemented, source support must be obtained separately and its participation and trading conditions must be supplemented by the upstream, and it must not be treated as an already implemented path."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G09","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The state-1 price formation scheme cites only [39], and the current frozen chain does not expand its internal formation rules. The initial average price step in R007 cannot replace the state-1 mid-market bid and ask price mechanism.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-pb","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-ps"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-M01-E24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"This cluster retains the state-1 bid and ask prices as existing inputs; if their price formation process is to be covered, the cited mechanism must be obtained and organized by the upstream, and it cannot be inferred backward from the initial average price."}]},"rule_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R003","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R007","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R001","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2d6ad9d125effd47","COMP-986a01fc4fcb352c","COMP-bfd4e5f3b6ab7697","COMP-c2c63e68e8427440","COMP-e02ca159eb62d0e4"]});
